{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":206233,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ec3e0bc7-1b50-48e7-9619-40453053068a","total_cost_usd":1.0923565,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65509,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"output_tokens":15318,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65509,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15318,"cache_read_input_tokens":16967,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65509,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65509},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45728,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.045822999999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15318,"cacheReadInputTokens":16967,"cacheCreationInputTokens":65509,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0465335,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flown, this config never reaches orbit — all three bands run out of fuel before circularising — and of the reentry claims that can still be checked, the parachute holds exactly while the pass-count optimum, the skim cooling, and the band difficulty ordering all fail, the last of them inverted: the high band is measured as the cheapest descent in the game.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ascent_does_not_close_in_any_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params balance_notes: exhaust velocity 3,000 m/s and wet/dry 3150/1350 give 2,542 m/s ideal dv against ~1,450 m/s (suborbital) and ~1,800 m/s (low), so 'both shipping-slice bands now close on ascent' with 75% and 40% margin.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Verification sweep, ascents: suborbital reached=false, low reached=false, high reached=false, all three 'out of fuel before circularising'. Reported fuel_remaining 503.73 / 377.44 / 248.37 kg (28% / 21% / 13.8%). Ideal-rocket-equation dv is not what the integrator spends: the ship is losing the difference to the climb. Every descent, ablation and economy figure in the params is conditioned on an orbit the ship does not achieve. Grid: bands_reachable is satisfied by 50% of the 5,184 configs, and every top-scoring world runs fuel_fraction 2.5-4.0 against this ship's 1800/1350 = 1.33.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cheapest_descent_is_single_pass_everywhere\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1: ablation is tuned so 'the cheapest path' is 2-4 committed passes, never a single plunge. game_params balance_note 5 concedes it cannot produce this and substitutes a skim-count optimum.\",\n      \"measured\": \"cheapest_pass_count = 1 in all nine band x load cases. Peak heat is nearly flat in pass count because braking altitude climbs as passes are added: suborbital empty 70 -> 74 while braking altitude goes 27,846 -> 38,424 m; high full hold 94 -> 108 across 22,450 -> 30,221 m. Cost is monotonically increasing from pass 1 in every case (suborbital empty 4.6 / 5.6 / 6.6 / 8.3%; high full hold 10.8 / 15.8 / 17.4 / 19.4%). The heat term has nothing to give back, so no assignment of cycle_toll_base_pct, cycle_toll_growth, heat_cost_coefficient or heat_cost_exponent moves the minimum off 1. This confirms GDD 4.5 risk 1 rather than clearing it: the U-curve does not exist inside a 43,000 m atmosphere. The decision is a human's — accept the skim framing into 2.3.1, or take the named fallback of flat per-pass ablation with a hard pass cap. Neither is a number I can nudge.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"difficulty_curve_inverts_with_altitude\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.7: 'the value curve and the risk curve rise together'; reentry heat scales with the altitude you return from. game_params cost_curve asserts minima of 6.21 / 12.78 / 32.03 plate-percent for suborbital / low / high, i.e. the high band costs 5.3x the suborbital one.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Flown, the ordering reverses. Cheapest ablation, empty: suborbital 4.6%, low 4.0%, high 3.6%. Full hold: 13.5% / 11.7% / 10.8%. Peak heat on the cheapest descent, empty: 70 / 67 / 64. The high band is the cheapest and coolest return in the game at every cargo load — the exact inversion GDD 4.5 risk 2 is written against, and it is measured, not predicted. (Held at a fixed entry depth the ordering is correct — see heat_index_high_overstated — so the inversion is produced by the descent solver braking higher bands deeper, not by the heat model.) Grid: difficulty_rises_with_band is satisfied by 60.8% of configs, so this is reachable; GDD 4.5 names the lever as band-gated ablation rates, which is what ablation.heat_index already is.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skimming_buys_almost_nothing_at_this_ballistic_coefficient\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params adopts skim_heat_multiplier [1, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958] and builds the entire anti-plunge substitution on it — three skims buying 4.2% of peak heat.\",\n      \"measured\": \"High band, entry_depth 0: [1, 0.99, 0.98, 0.972] — three skims buy 2.8%, a third less than the adopted array, and at entry_depth 21,500 m it degrades to [1, 0.994, 0.988, 0.983], 1.7%. Each skim costs commit_dv 44-45 m/s and 0.53 h of flight time. Entry depth by contrast moves heat 159.9 -> 90.9 (43% cooler) over the same 21,500 m — roughly 20x the leverage of the whole skim stack. The controlling quantity is the ballistic coefficient: the sweep reports staged 290.3 kg/m2, while the grid worlds where skimming genuinely cools run beta 33-133 and reach [1, 0.925, 0.849, 0.766] or better. Grid: skimming_cools_the_entry satisfied by 43.8% of configs, so this is tuning, not an impossible rule.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optimal_skims_high_is_one_not_two\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params ablation.optimal_skims.high = 2, derived from totals 33.13 / 32.31 / 32.03 / 32.61 with a stated 0.28 plate-percent separation.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Re-running the params' own arithmetic on the measured multipliers [1, 0.99, 0.98, 0.972] at heat_index 138: heat terms 32.85 / 31.88 / 30.92 / 30.17, tolls 0.28 / 0.784 / 1.691 / 3.324, skim heat 0 / 0.133 / 0.266 / 0.399, totals 33.13 / 32.80 / 32.88 / 33.89. The minimum moves to 1 skim, and 0 vs 1 are separated by 0.33 plate-percent. At the corrected heat_index of 128 the totals are 26.49 / 26.36 / 26.63 / 27.79 — still 1. The optimum is inside the required 1-2 window either way, but the stated value is wrong and the margin is thinner than a rounding error on the plate gauge.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"heat_index_high_overstated_not_understated\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params heat_index 78 / 100 / 138, with balance_note 8 worrying the high band is '17% low' against a reported 161.5 peak and asking for it to be routed as its own finding.\",\n      \"measured\": \"It is routed, and it points the other way. At a fixed entry depth of 0 with no skims, an empty ship peaks at 100 (suborbital) / 125 (low) / 159.9 (high) on the sweep's bar, which is normalised to suborbital = 100. Renormalised to the params' own convention of low = 100, the measured indices are 80 / 100 / 127.9 against the stated 78 / 100 / 138. The high band is 7.9% overstated; suborbital is 2.6% understated. The 161.5 figure the note was reacting to is on the suborbital-normalised scale, which is what made it look 17% low.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parachute_claim_holds_exactly\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params descent_speed_full_hold_ms = 4.59, derived from 870 m2 at Cd 1.8 against a 2,747.8 kg full-hold ship.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Independently measured at 4.59 m/s, delta 0, spread across bands 0. Touchdown is 3.22 / 3.96 / 4.59 m/s at empty / half / full hold and soft_landing = true in all nine descents. full_hold_mass_ratio measured 2.04 against the claimed 2.035, inside the 1.75-2.25 window. This is the one claim in the file the simulator confirms to the digit. Worth knowing that the margin is 0.41 m/s and that only 31.5% of grid configs satisfy full_hold_lands_soft at all — storage tier 1 spends most of what is left.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_pass_survives_here_and_almost_nowhere_else\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1: shallow unstaged passes are survivable and are how coarse pre-stage braking happens; unstaged_heat_multiplier = 3.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Holds in this world: shallow unstaged pass peaks at 54 (suborbital) and 60 (low), both survivable against a 100 capacity. But the grid satisfies unstaged_pass_survivable in only 7.4% of 5,184 configs, and every one of the twelve top-scoring worlds fails it, at unstaged peak heats of 356-419. This is the one target the crew's config wins and the grid's best worlds lose, which is the reason not to adopt a top-scoring grid world wholesale.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reported_ballistic_coefficient_is_at_dry_mass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"game_params balance_note 9 computes staged full-hold beta = 2747.8 / 4.65 = 591 kg/m2 and flags it as above the Researcher's 300-500 capsule band.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The sweep reports staged 290.3 and unstaged 967.7 kg/m2. Both back-solve to 1,350 kg (290.3 x 1.5 x 3.1 and 967.7 x 0.45 x 3.1), so the reported figure is the dry, empty, fuel-less ship — not the same quantity the params quote. The two do not disagree about physics; the descents plainly do carry cargo mass, since peak heat moves 70 -> 102 from empty to full hold. Both figures sit far above the ~50 kg/m2 floor below which aerobraking cannot exist, so the mechanic is intact — but any beta comparison between the params and the sweep is currently comparing two different ships.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 1800,\n      \"proposed\": 3400,\n      \"reason\": \"Takes fuel fraction from 1.33 to 2.52, into the 2.5-4.0 band every bands_reachable grid config occupies, and ideal dv from 2,542 to 3,775 m/s; it costs liftoff TWR (see the thrust change) and it puts both fuel_tank upgrade tiers, at 2,300 and 2,900, below the new base, so that ladder has to be re-emitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.thrust_n\",\n      \"current\": 78000,\n      \"proposed\": 118000,\n      \"reason\": \"Restores liftoff TWR to 2.76 at the new 4,750 kg wet mass — the balance_notes already identify low TWR as where the previous ascent lost its dv to hovering — and it costs the thruster upgrade ladder, whose 92,000 and 108,000 tiers now sit below base and must be re-priced above it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.reference_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 3.1,\n      \"proposed\": 6.0,\n      \"reason\": \"In baseline.json: halves the ballistic coefficient toward the 33-133 kg/m2 range where the grid measures skims actually cooling (0.766-0.849 over three skims, against 0.972 here), which is the only lever that makes the skim substitution in balance_note 5 worth flying; it costs the Researcher's stated symmetry between hull and shield area and will shorten every descent, so the whole descent table needs re-flying rather than re-deriving.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958],\n      \"proposed\": [1, 0.99, 0.98, 0.972],\n      \"reason\": \"The measured high-band array at entry_depth 0; the flown value is the truth and the adopted one overstates three skims' cooling by a third, which costs nothing but the cost_curve, which has to be re-emitted with it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.optimal_skims.high\",\n      \"current\": 2,\n      \"proposed\": 1,\n      \"reason\": \"Under the measured multipliers the totals become 33.13 / 32.80 / 32.88 / 33.89 and the minimum moves to one skim; it stays inside the required 1-2 window, but the 0.33 plate-percent separation should be stated as the thin margin it is.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_index.high\",\n      \"current\": 138,\n      \"proposed\": 128,\n      \"reason\": \"Measured at a fixed entry depth the high band reads 127.9 against low = 100, not 138; correcting it settles the open question in balance_note 8 in the opposite direction to the one it guessed, and it lowers the whole high-band cost_curve by roughly 20%.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.heat_index.suborbital\",\n      \"current\": 78,\n      \"proposed\": 80,\n      \"reason\": \"Same measurement, same normalisation — suborbital reads 80 against low = 100; a 2.6% correction that costs nothing and keeps all three indices on one measured scale.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The ascent finding is load-bearing and the sweep is internally inconsistent about it: it reports 'out of fuel before circularising' alongside 503.73 kg remaining and a 28% margin. Both cannot be literal. I trust reached=false — it is the flag the descent cases are all conditioned on — and I would not quote the 28% figure to anyone until someone says what budget it is a margin against.\",\n    \"The descent series and the skim series disagree in sign about band difficulty: descents get cooler with altitude (70 / 67 / 64) while fixed-depth entries get hotter (100 / 125 / 159.9). The difference is entry depth, which the descent solver floats and the skim series pins. This is exactly the confusion the charter warns about, so I have kept them apart: the inversion finding is about what the descent solver does, and the heat_index finding is about what the heat model does. Neither should be quoted as evidence for the other.\",\n    \"The Researcher predicts a 1.31x band-to-band heat spread from v-cubed at a common periapsis; the simulator measures 1.60x at a common entry depth. I have not reconciled these and I would not assume the simulator's heat model is the Researcher's. The heat bar is a normalised 0-100 scale by the sweep's own statement, so every heat figure I have quoted is relative, and none of it is W/m2.\",\n    \"The fuel and thrust proposals are derived from the grid's fuel_fraction and TWR distributions plus the rocket equation, not from a flown re-run of this ship. They are the direction the evidence points, not a measured fix, and they must be re-swept before anyone believes the specific numbers. They also invalidate the fuel_tank and thruster upgrade ladders, which is the economy-balancer's work and not mine.\",\n    \"The reference_area change moves the quantity that controls whether skimming exists at all, but 6.0 m2 is chosen to land near the grid's cooling band, not measured. It also raises unstaged drag, which currently has comfortable margin (54 and 60 against a 100 capacity) but is satisfied by only 7.4% of the grid — if the re-sweep shows unstaged peaks climbing toward 100, this is the change to back off first.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot. off_retrograde_penalty, the cosine heat rule, chute-shred timing against the plasma cue, latch and swing jerk, debris collisions, and everything in the tether model are untested by anything I have seen — no finding above rests on them, and the cryo_propellant_sphere concern the economy-balancer raised remains open, not cleared.\",\n    \"None of the top-scoring grid worlds is a drop-in replacement. They vary planet radius and gravity, which the design has fixed elsewhere, and all twelve fail unstaged_pass_survivable at peaks of 356-419 where the crew's config sits at 54-60. I have used the grid only to separate tuning problems from design ones, which is what the satisfaction rates are for.\",\n    \"I cannot say whether any of this is fun. The plasma-to-chute window, whether a 0.41 m/s parachute margin reads as tense or as luck, and whether one skim feels like a decision or like arithmetic are the human's checkpoints 2 and 3, and nothing in the sweep touches them.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":130680,"ttft_stream_ms":1884,"time_to_request_ms":210,"type":"result","duration_ms":203705,"uuid":"cd4259ef-88c9-4075-a46a-e97d447c6278"}
